📋 Compliance & Frameworks
Compliance and best practices guide the selection of security controls:
• 	Regulatory Compliance: Laws like GDPR, HIPAA, or PCI-DSS require specific protections.
• 	Frameworks: Standards like NIST, ISO/IEC 27001, and CIS Controls help organizations structure their security programs.
• 	Best Practices: Industry-accepted methods for securing systems and data.
These frameworks ensure consistency, accountability, and legal adherence across organizations.

🏢 Security Roles & Responsibilities
Security is implemented differently across organizations, but common roles include:
• 	CISO (Chief Information Security Officer): Oversees the entire security strategy.
• 	Security Analysts: Monitor systems and respond to incidents.
• 	Security Engineers: Build and maintain secure infrastructure.
• 	Compliance Officers: Ensure adherence to laws and standards.
• 	IT Departments: Often collaborate with security teams to enforce controls.
Departments and units tailor their security functions based on size, industry, and risk profile.
